---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="How posts on Deals For Moms are researched, verified, corrected, and disclosed.">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:48px">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
      <h2>Every post is verified in person</h2>
      <p>A deal post does not go live without a first-hand element: a photo of the shelf tag, a receipt, or a screenshot from the Walmart app taken at the store. That evidence is named at the bottom of every post.</p>
      <h2>AI is a drafting tool, not a source</h2>
      <p>I use AI tools to help research, structure and draft articles, the same way a writer uses an editor. Facts, prices and dates come from stores and from primary sources — never from a model, and never scraped and republished from another site. Every post is reviewed by me before it publishes.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>When a post is wrong, I fix it and note what changed and when, rather than quietly editing. Updated posts show an updated date.</p>
      <h2>Money</h2>
      <p>Affiliate links pay for this site. Nothing else does. See the <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> for the full picture.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
